Prompt: 
2x2 grid, give it for 4 stories parents tell their children in various countries, 16:9        INPUT: $ TOPIC 
// Narrative model
TYPE = classify($ TOPIC)
WORD = derive_display_word($ TOPIC)
PROTAGONIST = infer_primary_avatar($ TOPIC)
CAST = infer_supporting_cast($ TOPIC)
SETTING = infer_world_setting($ TOPIC)
MATERIALS = infer_native_materials($ TOPIC)
THEME = infer_story_theme($ TOPIC)
ORIGIN = infer_origin_if_relevant($ TOPIC)

// Build environmental potential field Φ across the illustrated page.
Φ = landscape_energy(SETTING) + protagonist_gravity(PROTAGONIST) + material_texture(MATERIALS)
F = ∇Φ       // composition flow: reading direction, protagonist path
Curl = ∇×Φ   // watercolor pigment swirl, wind, water currents
Div = ∇·F    // density of supporting cast, small props, decorative marks

// Glyph construction:
// For each letter L in WORD:
//   search MATERIALS ∪ SETTING for a shape or element that visually matches L
//   (e.g., mountain ridge, river bend, tree branch, arch of a bridge, curling smoke)
//   Replace flat typography with the chosen glyph source, embedded in the terrain.
// The word must read as a single monumental environmental form.

// Composition:
// - Word occupies the central horizontal band of the page, embedded in the landscape.
// - Protagonist stands at a focal point; supporting cast scattered at smaller scale.
// - Setting extends beyond the word, framed by pigment splashes and organic paper bleed.

// Style:
// - Watercolor washes, ink contour lines, handmade folklore travel journal.
// - Palette drawn from MATERIALS + SETTING; warm earth tones, muted pigments.
// - Edge behavior: pigment splashes, paper bleed, faded fiber.

// Typography overlays:
// - Upper annotation: short poetic epigram derived from THEME.
// - Lower annotation: NAME and ORIGIN.

// Scoring: choose variant with maximum storytelling_strength,
// glyph_world_integration, cultural_specificity, painterly_detail, poster_readability.
Render one illustration, 1:1 or 4:5.

